WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.230
 

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:04.980
imagine ...

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.500
a soldier

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:09.856
the size of an insect

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.920
the ultimate secret weapon

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.620
if you give God-like powers to everyone

00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:19.394
It's going to be chaos

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.926
So how do we stop him?

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:22.700
I know a guy.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:27.640
Scott

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.128
I've been watching for a while

00:00:31.694 --> 00:00:32.734
you're different

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.460
and I believe everyone deserves a shot at redemption

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.580
Do you?

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:40.780
absolutely

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.680
my days of breaking into places and stealing stuff

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:44.903
are over

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.980
What do you want me to do?

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.820
I want you to break into a place and steal some stuff

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:51.974
makes sense

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.780
Are you ready

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.626
to become the hero?

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.774
Now the suit has powers

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.480
You have to learn how to control it

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.860
and these are your greatest allies

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:09.880
You're kind of cute!

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.000
Whoa!

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.500
when you're small

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.200
have super-human strength

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.360
you're like a bullet

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.860
so you need to know how to punch

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.720
you're wanna show me how to punch?

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:24.555
show me how to punch...

00:01:26.357 --> 00:01:27.717
that's how you punch.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.620
you tried to to hide your suit me

00:01:34.795 --> 00:01:36.715
Now, it's going to blow up in your face

00:01:37.224 --> 00:01:39.704
and destroy everyone you care about

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.360
Scott, get out of there!

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.260
Did you think you could stop the future

00:01:50.894 --> 00:01:52.334
you're just a thief

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:53.600
NO

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.500
I'm Ant-Man

00:01:56.018 --> 00:01:57.638
I know, it wasn't my idea

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.940
Hey YouTubers it's Charlie

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.060
So new Ant-Man trailer 

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.560
so this is gonna be a breakdown video

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.800
I'll also explain how it fits into MCU

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.740
Marvel just did an Age of Ultron press conference

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:29.740
where they gave out a lot of details about

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.580
of you know, thematically

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.393
where Ant-Man is supposed to fit with all these big Avengers films

00:02:33.393 --> 00:02:34.613
 

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.640
so 6 billion dollar question

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.760
where does this movie fit in with all the other big stuff

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.267
Kevin Feige said that this is like a bookend for phase 2

00:02:42.267 --> 00:02:43.320
its like a different kind of book end 

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:45.540
because technically Age of Ultron

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.940
is the last phase 2 film

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.088
what this does

00:02:48.088 --> 00:02:49.852
is fill in the lot of gaps

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.412
of 60's 70's and 80's in the marvel universe

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.580
Movies and TV Shows

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.680
haven't spend a lot of time in those decades

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.025
like we see  in Agent Carter

00:02:58.061 --> 00:02:59.581
which is like the beginning

00:02:59.581 --> 00:03:01.171
but we haven't seen the lot of middle stuff

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.380
thats when the Hank Pym's character comes in

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.120
so you learn a lot what's been happening

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.920
between agent carter and the first iron man film

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:10.420
The film itself takes place after Avengers Age of Ultron

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:13.620
they said that a lot of the decisions Hank Pym

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.913
makes in the movie are based on what happens at the end of Age of Ultron

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.140
I think the same thing can be said for  Yellowjacket the villain here

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.080
this trailer really explains the story of the movie

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.620
in a much bigger way than the previous trailers have

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.300
Yellowjacket is now the head of Pym's company

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.240
Pym is like the old man that's kinda been pushed out

00:03:29.514 --> 00:03:30.574
His daughter, Hope Van Dyne,

00:03:30.574 --> 00:03:33.280
very much involved with the day to day stuff

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.620
Imagine a punchier, kickier version of  Pepper Potts

00:03:36.155 --> 00:03:36.955
Evangeline Lilly

00:03:36.955 --> 00:03:38.834
awesome in the Hobbit movies,

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.157
I think she has high potential

00:03:40.157 --> 00:03:41.797
to wind up in a future Avengers film.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:42.520
Like in Avengers 3

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:43.820
What I'm hoping is

00:03:43.885 --> 00:03:47.005
is that once they steal back the Yellowjacket suit, 

00:03:47.005 --> 00:03:48.285
they'll modify it and she'll wear that

00:03:48.285 --> 00:03:49.485
and become The Wasp

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.680
I know everybody misses Janet Van Dyne

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.500
but they said they would explain where she is in this movie

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.634
Most of these tech-looking shots are from inside Pym Tech

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.753
with the exception of Hank Pym's lab

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.560
They do a good job of showing the scale of like how Ant-Man

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.420
gets stronger as he gets smaller

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.480
It's the same principle behind the strength of ants

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.340
So he can kick the shit out of people when he's super small

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.380
Even though he's a weakling when he's normal sized.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:15.293
A big thing about the movie, and what's going to lead up into Avengers 3

00:04:15.293 --> 00:04:18.258
is that even regular people can be heroes, too

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:21.518
That's kind of what's going on in Daredevil right now, you know, street-level heroes

00:04:21.737 --> 00:04:23.577
Scott Lang is just another twist on that

00:04:23.577 --> 00:04:25.436
even dirt bags can be heroes

00:04:25.436 --> 00:04:26.835
I don't know if I'd call him a dirt bag, 

00:04:26.835 --> 00:04:29.815
but I think it's a better description of where his character starts out

00:04:29.815 --> 00:04:31.794
The movie explains his origin story

00:04:32.118 --> 00:04:34.598
about how he steals to support his daughter

00:04:34.598 --> 00:04:36.538
So he's a dirt bag out of necessity

00:04:36.538 --> 00:04:38.695
As they explain, Yellowjacket's plan

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.120
is to create an army of ANTMEN

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:43.658
in order to do that he needs Pym particles

00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:46.843
like, you can build the suits, but in order to shrink you need the Pym particles

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.600
He appropriates that from Pym

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.940
their disagreement over that is what leads to the heist

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.340
I love all these Hank Pym scenes - like this in Pym's lab. You get a sense that he's

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.900
been doing this for a long time

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.075
He's been the Ant-Man for a long time

00:05:00.075 --> 00:05:02.635
That's why the Yellowjacket suit looks more contemporary

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.456
And the Ant-Man suit looks like it was built 20 years ago

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.220
Whenever you guys go to see the movie

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.480
make sure that in all these Hank Pym Lab scenes

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.760
you keep your eyes peeled

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.933
They're probably full of Easter Eggs 

00:05:11.933 --> 00:05:15.753
If you're a hardcore Hank Pym Ant-Man fan, these will really be your moments

00:05:15.753 --> 00:05:19.313
It's like in GAME OF THRONES where they tell you about Robert's Rebellion

00:05:19.313 --> 00:05:23.369
this big adventure that you don't see, they just tell you about it after the fact

00:05:23.369 --> 00:05:27.109
Hanks Pym probably explain what made the past 20 years

00:05:27.109 --> 00:05:28.429
with the Ant-Man technology.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.344
I'll be interested to see how true his character is to his comic book character

00:05:32.344 --> 00:05:35.992
because I always thought of him as like a crazier, mad version of Tony Stark

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:38.480
Like Tony Stark with grayer morality.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.100
All these really small size scenes do a really good job of showing the scale.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.620
You have the real world shrunk down here

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.420
and then in the other ant-based scenes

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:48.660
you see him inside an ant farm

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.700
really the hard sell of this movie, isn't so much the suit

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.660
we understand super suits - shrinking isn't that big of a leap

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.220
It's really his ability to communicate with Ants that they need to explain

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.654
I feel like if you read comics, it's not a big deal - you totally get it.

00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:04.428
you're like, "Ok he can talk to ants"

00:06:04.428 --> 00:06:07.856
the problem with big Marvel movies is that they have to explain this stuff

00:06:07.856 --> 00:06:09.545
to people who have never read comics before

00:06:09.545 --> 00:06:11.380
they're like "Why is he talking to ants? I don't get it"

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.080
I like that Hope tells him he's kind of like a bullet when he's small

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.620
like he's as strong as a bullet

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:20.133
It seems like they're trying to build some sort of relationship between the two characters

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:22.996
which is why they went with Hope instead of Janet, I think

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.360
It's a nice twist on the Pepper Potts/Tony Stark relationship

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.253
This is a nice shot of them messing with Pym particles 

00:06:29.253 --> 00:06:32.453
I'm looking forward to seeing how the movies explain those, versus the comics

00:06:32.835 --> 00:06:35.303
The comics are a little opaque with the way they explain them

00:06:35.303 --> 00:06:37.583
There's this new type of particle that allows you to do these things

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:41.140
It is like inventing Vibranium because you need a super strong metal

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.720
they don't get too deep into the mechanics of Vibranium

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.700
it's just like a one sentence explainer

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.280
super strong metal... okay, we get it.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.980
I think this train scene was inspired by the LEGO movie

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.440
probably the most funniest moment in a Marvel trailer

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:54.500
that I've seen in a long time

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.200
aside from science-bro-fist

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.260
really, the job of this movie is to sell the Scott Lang character.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:04.660
They can do action great - Marvel has action down 100%, that's the easy part,

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.160
The hard part is making us believe that Scott Lang could go toe-to-toe with Tony Stark, Thor,

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.300
all the other Avenger characters.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.600
or that he even deserves to be in their company

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.180
But as you can see from this train scene

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.140
This is probably going to be the funniest Marvel movie that you've seen so far

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:21.890
I mean, Avengers Age of Ultron has a lot of funny moments

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.300
Joss Whedon is a comedic genius

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:27.400
but from the ground up, Ant-Man is built more on comedy than I think the Avengers are

00:07:27.917 --> 00:07:30.637
Speaking of which, transitioning into Avengers Age of Ultron stuff

